Start_PP: parameter scans for the parallel-parameters mode (PP) of ALF
=======================================================================

prepare_sim.py turns ONE template `parameters` file, in which some parameters are given as sets of values,
into one directory Temp_<i>/ per combination of values. ALF compiled with PP (configure.sh ... PP ...)
then runs all of them in one MPI job: mpi_per_parameter_set ranks per Temp_<i>. The same layout is used
by parallel tempering (TEMPERING), see ../Start_Tempering.

Files
  parameters          example template (lattice-size scan with linked N_Phi and Beta, U scan)
  prepare_sim.py      the generator (needs f90nml: pip install f90nml; pyALF installs it too)
  seeds               one integer seed per MPI rank (needs at least as many lines as ranks)
  out_to_in_temper.sh renames confout_* to confin_* in every Temp_*/ before a continuation run

Usage
  python3 prepare_sim.py [-t TEMPLATE] [-o OUTDIR] [--no-links]
  python3 prepare_sim.py --self-test       # generates a built-in example in a temp dir and checks it
  python3 prepare_sim.py --help
Defaults: TEMPLATE = ./parameters, OUTDIR = . (as the original script, which took no arguments).

Template syntax
  ham_U = {0.5d0, 1.5d0, 3.0d0}              set: one simulation per value
  L2    = [4, 6, 8; VAR_lattice, L1]         linked list: element i goes with element i of the set
                                             VAR_lattice/L1 (same length); it does not add combinations
  everything else                            copied unchanged
Independent sets are combined as a Cartesian product. ham_name = {"Hubbard", "tV"} is allowed; the sets in
VAR_Hubbard (VAR_tV) are only varied for ham_name = "Hubbard" ("tV"); the rules are in RULES in
prepare_sim.py. VAR_errors and VAR_Max_Stoch are never varied.
For every combination the script writes OUTDIR/Temp_<i>/parameters and a symbolic link named after the
varied values (e.g. ham_name_Hubbard_ham_u_0.5_l1_6_l2_6_beta_6_n_phi_18 -> Temp_<i>), and prints the
number of sets and the required number of MPI ranks.

Worked example: U scan of the Hubbard model, 4 values of U, 2 independent walkers (ranks) per U
  mkdir run && cd run
  cp $ALF_DIR/Scripts_and_Parameters_files/Start_PP/{parameters,seeds,prepare_sim.py} .
  # edit parameters:
  #   &VAR_lattice  L1 = 6,  L2 = 6                    (scalars: no lattice scan)
  #   &VAR_Model_Generic  N_Phi = 0, Beta = 5.d0
  #   &VAR_TEMP     mpi_per_parameter_set = 2, N_exchange_steps = 0
  #   &VAR_Hubbard  ham_U = {2.d0, 4.d0, 6.d0, 8.d0}
  python3 prepare_sim.py
  #   -> 4 parameter sets written to ./Temp_<i>; mpi_per_parameter_set = 2: run with mpiexec -n 8
  mpiexec -n 8 $ALF_DIR/Prog/ALF.out
Rank r writes to Temp_<r / mpi_per_parameter_set>/. To continue: ./out_to_in_temper.sh, then run again.
The example template as shipped scans L = 4, 6, 8 (with N_Phi = L^2/2 and Beta = L linked to L1) times
7 values of U: 21 sets.

Notes
  * mpi_per_parameter_set is read from &VAR_TEMP of the top-level parameters; the number of ranks must be
    (number of Temp_<i>) * mpi_per_parameter_set.
  * Runs with different Beta or lattice size in one job take different times per bin; use CPU_MAX with a
    large NBin, or scan only parameters that do not change the cost.

Related tools (model-specific, not general generators; they write the same Temp_<i> layout):
  ../make_PP_Uscan.py                      point-defect Hubbard U scan, stdlib only, can fill a jobfile
  ../Start_PP_GPU/make_pp_dirs.py          same model, GPU production defaults
  docs/gpu/scripts/pp/pp_setup.py          nividia helper that runs prepare_sim.py on a generated template
docs/gpu/scripts/pp/prepare_sim.py is a symbolic link to this prepare_sim.py.
